From: mhasseli1987 <mhasseli1987@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:46:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/25] Click the ten rounds after a high round and keep tabs
 readable when narrow
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The clicker used the multiplier as a per-round gate, so the rounds following a
high result were skipped whenever they closed low; a high round now arms a run
of the next autoclick_max_clicks rounds and each of them clicks the region
whatever it closes at. Dashboard and calibration tabs sit in scroll areas with a
minimum content width and wrapped captions, so shrinking the window scrolls
instead of collapsing the Persian text onto itself.

