From cccadef38390af551f49ab38d2029e91877afa39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Buffy <buffy@freebuff.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:47:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/25] Delay every auto-click by a second and keep a run at
 ten clicks

Clicks fired the moment the Bang screen appeared sometimes landed before the
site accepted input, and a second high round restarted the run instead of
letting it finish its ten clicks. Clicks now wait one second (a floor enforced
on load) and only an idle clicker starts a run.
---
 README.md                        |  8 +++++---
 crash_watcher/desktop/clicker.py | 14 +++++++-------
 crash_watcher/desktop/config.py  |  9 ++++++++-
 crash_watcher/desktop/ui.py      | 10 ++++++----
 tests/test_desktop.py            | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 5 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 27f9d90..7ed115d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -7,9 +7,11 @@ Windows distribution.
 
 Python 3.11+ YELLOW HUNTER simulation engine with local screen recognition
 and a Windows desktop interface. Auto-click is off by default: a confirmed round at or above
-the click threshold is clicked and starts a run in which the next `autoclick_max_clicks`
-rounds (default 10) each click the saved region whatever they close at; a new high round
-restarts the run. Both label modes click — the mode button only marks the log entry.
+the click threshold starts a run of exactly `autoclick_max_clicks` clicks (default 10),
+regardless of what the rounds in between close at; another high round inside the run does
+not reset the count, and the run restarts only after its ten clicks are spent. Each click
+waits `autoclick_delay_ms` (default 1000 ms, minimum one second) after the round closes so
+the site registers it. Both label modes click — the mode button only marks the log entry.
 
 ## Windows setup and execution
 
