--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -13,6 +13,17 @@ not reset the count, and the run restarts only after its ten clicks are spent. E
 waits `autoclick_delay_ms` (default 1000 ms, minimum one second) after the round closes so
 the site registers it. Both label modes click — the mode button only marks the log entry.
 
+**Smart click (opt-in).** With `smart_click_enabled` the clicker first forecasts the next
+dot color from the recent color mix and the color that used to follow the previous one
+(`desktop/forecast.py`); it only clicks when that forecast reaches
+`prediction_min_confidence` (default 0.60) and enough rounds have been seen, otherwise the
+round is skipped. The ten-click run after a high round still fires unconditionally. Every
+`review_window_s` (default 600 s) it writes a review row (rounds, clicks, skips, forecast
+hit rate, model accuracies) to `logs/reviews.csv` and shows it in the calibration tab, so the
+forecast is judged by measurement instead of belief. The game draws independent rounds, so
+expect the model to sit near the base rates (red ≈ 50%, green ≈ 40%, yellow ≈ 10%) most of
+the time.
+
 ## Windows setup and execution
 
